Virtual Pet Game
README
Authors: Jasmine Pruzan, Ishaan Bhalerao, Ellie Lo
Version: June 2026
Language: Java | GUI: Java Swing

================================================================

OVERVIEW

Virtual Pet Game is a desktop Java application where players adopt and care for a digital pet of their choice: a Dog, a Cat, or a Fish. The goal of the game is to keep your companion happy and healthy by managing five interconnected vital statistics: health, hunger, emotion, rest, and hygiene.

The game features a realistic financial system where players must balance a budget. Actions like feeding or playing cost money, and total expenditures are tracked live. To support your pet's lifestyle, you can earn money by completing tasks or financial literacy quizzes, adding an educational layer to your pet care routine. The game ends if your pet's vitals are neglected, leading to a final session summary where you can review your financial choices and export your records.

================================================================

GETTING STARTED

Prerequisites:

Java 11 or higher

The external org.json library dependency added to your project's build path (required for processing question and item data structures)

A Java-supported IDE (such as Eclipse, IntelliJ IDEA, or VS Code)

To run the application:

Download or clone the project source files.

Open the project folder inside your Java IDE.

Ensure the external library (org.json JAR) is added to your project's build path.

Make sure your asset files are placed in their respective asset resource folders (e.g., Images/Pet_Sprites/ and Images/Toy_Icons/).

Run the main class file to launch the application.

Follow the on-screen setup prompts to create your player profile, name your new pet, and pick its species.

================================================================

PROJECT STRUCTURE

pets
Contains the Pet class, which serves as the core data model holding all live data variables including stats, wallet balances, and inventory slots.

panels
Contains the user interface screen panels and custom dialog setups for the marketplace modules (StorePanel and StorePanelFood), the earning screens, and the post-game data ledger.

properties
Contains the primary game simulation logic, calculation engines, and blueprint definitions: Food, Toy, Store, Activities, Health, and Emotion.

DrawingSurface
Contains the top-level GUI container, graphics rendering hooks, custom background panels, layout manager files, and visual button styles.

================================================================

CLASS REFERENCE

Pet (pets.Pet)
The primary data hub of the application. It acts as the single source of truth for your pet's current state. It initializes your pet with its name and animal type, tracks the active balance in your wallet, logs total accrued expenses, and holds arrays of purchased items. All five vital stats range from 0 to 10. The core setter methods automatically cap values at a maximum of 10 and trigger real-time updates across dependent stat systems.

Health (properties.Health)
Monages how changes in hunger, rest, and hygiene passively impact your pet's overall health bar. If core needs like hunger drop to zero, health decreases rapidly. When needs are well-maintained, health slowly recovers over time. If your pet's health drops to 2 or below, normal items can no longer restore it; the system locks standard recovery and displays an urgent notification window warning you that an immediate veterinary visit is required.

Emotion (properties.Emotion)
Calculates your companion's general happiness and mood behavior. It dynamically reads your pet's current vitals to update their emotional status. If any vital statistic falls to 3 or below, emotion is automatically forced to a low level, causing the pet's sprite graphic to change to a sad face. If all physical needs are successfully maintained at 7 or above, your pet receives a massive happiness boost and updates to a happy animation frame.

Food (properties.Food)
Defines purchasable food items, tracking their name, price, target animal type, and quality tier. When you feed your pet an item that matches its species, its hunger meter is replenished according to the item's quality level. However, if you feed a pet the wrong item type (such as giving fish flakes to a dog), the pet only receives half of the nutritional value, and its health decreases due to an incompatible diet.

Available Dog Food:

Kibble Crunch ($10.00)

Salmon Delight ($50.00)

Gold Nuggets ($100.00)

Available Fish Food:

Flakes ($10.00)

Algae Crisps ($50.00)

Abyss Infusion ($100.00)

Available Cat Food:

Fish Kibble ($10.00)

Turkey Treats ($50.00)

A Golden Rat ($100.00)

Toy (properties.Toy)
Defines interactive items that can be bought, collected, and stored within your pet's inventory. Playing with toys is the primary method for raising your pet's emotion level. Like food items, toys are categorized by species type and tier level to ensure appropriate playtime interactions.

Available Dog Toys:

Used Ball ($4.00)

Chew Wand ($25.00)

Gold Bone ($90.00)

Available Fish Toys:

Drift Ball ($4.00)

Bubble Maker ($25.00)

Super Speaker ($90.00)

Available Cat Toys:

Plain Sock ($4.00)

Laser Pointer ($50.00)

Rad Airpods ($90.00)

Store (properties.Store)
The overarching management system for all in-game commerce. It retains complete item registries and processes every shopping transaction securely.

buyFood(): Checks if you have enough money, deducts the price from your wallet, updates your cumulative expenses, and triggers an immediate feeding action.

buyToys(): Verifies inventory capacity limits, deducts funds, updates expense tracking, and places the newly acquired item into an open inventory slot.

vetVisit(): Processes an emergency medical care transaction for a flat rate of $20.00, automatically restoring your pet's health to 10. If your bank balance is under $20.00, the visit is rejected.

StorePanel & StorePanelFood (panels)
The marketplace graphic interfaces handled via absolute custom layouts. They present item choices as custom compound buttons showing item prices, levels, and icons. Both shop screens feature a transparent live status overlay at the top right of the screen. This layout draws real-time data updates directly from the active Pet object, instantly refreshing your available balance and total amount spent every time a purchase is made.

DrawingSurface (DrawingSurface.DrawingSurface)
The central visual coordinator for the game's interface. Built on top of a CardLayout setup, it handles seamless panel swapping between the home screen, work applications, and marketplace layouts. It listens for user menu interactions and coordinates smooth communication between your visual buttons and the underlying game properties data.

================================================================

STAT SYSTEM SUMMARY

All internal game stats operate strictly on a scale from 0 to 10.

Health   - Governed by basic lifestyle metrics (hunger, sleep, cleanliness). Requires an explicit vet visit to fix if it degrades past safe thresholds.
Hunger   - Automatically drains over time. Restored by purchasing and matching correct species-specific food items from the shop.
Emotion  - Reflects the general state of your pet's physical conditions and increases during play actions.
Rest     - Slowly drops while your pet is awake. Restored by putting your pet to sleep for chosen hour durations.
Hygiene  - Gradually decays as time ticks forward. Restored by executing clean and grooming actions.

================================================================

SESSION SUMMARY AND DATA EXPORT

When you choose to exit the application or when your pet's vitals drop to zero, the game transitions to a comprehensive post-game analytical review panel. This screen functions as a financial ledger that outlines your session performance, detailing your final wallet standings, savings efficiency, and a complete itemized shopping receipt. The receipt checker evaluates your purchases and highlights whether items were a "Good Match" or a "No Match" for your pet's species.

To help you track your budgeting habits over time, this ledger includes built-in file export drivers. With a single click, you can save your entire session history to your desktop as a clean CSV spreadsheet or a styled HTML webpage report.